Module tallow "Tallow Deep" {
  // ── Keeping ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What the hill is about: things kept after the reason for keeping them has gone. The makers' weight is kept
  // swinging by figures that wind it; the Aeneans kept a cap over what they could not read; the Company kept its dead
  // in a vault and its secret in a desk; the Tallymen keep a road they did not make; the village keeps its back
  // turned. Each of them is answerable to something it will not look at.
  Relation namesRead(group). Relation ticked(group).

  Chapter ch_swallet "The Village That Does Not Look" when true "Swallet keeps its back to the ridge. Everyone in it can tell you the way in, and nobody will tell you why they stopped going.".
  Chapter ch_dayl "The Company's Works" when been(party, adit) "The Brasiers left in a season, and left their tools hanging. Other people have been living in their leavings since.".
  Chapter ch_cistern "What the Legion Capped" when been(party, cistern_hall) "A hall built to settle a river, and, in the middle of it, a lid.".
  Chapter ch_bore "The Weight" when been(party, breach) "Under the lid there is a stair, and at the bottom of the stair something has been counting for longer than there have been people to count for.".

  // A tick under the pipe, from the first day: the figure in the Bore is six breaths.
  Observe pipe_tick at green as sound when true "Under the gurgle of the pipe, so faint you take it for your own pulse, something ticks: once, and again, six breaths apart.".
  Observe shaft_tick at winding as sound when true "Under the water far below the cage there is a tick, and a tick, evenly, not a drip. It has the patience of a thing that does not mind who is listening.".
  Topic dunstan_tick with dunstan "Ask Dunstan about the ticking under the pipe" when true {
    Says "'You hear it, then,' says Dunstan. 'Not many do. We heard it in the shaft the winter before the shot, and the Foreman had us stop work to listen, and it kept time, and not ours.' He drinks. 'Carr said the Legion's engineers heard it too. He'd read their wall. He said they were the first people who had the sense to be afraid of it, and the only ones who had the sense to leave it running.'".
  }

  // The Foreman's ledger: fourteen names and the wages owed them.
  Topic joss_father with joss "Show Joss the fourteen names in the Foreman's ledger" when holding(actor, carr_ledger) and not namesRead(party) once {
    Says "Joss reads down the column with a clerk's finger, and stops at the ninth. TARBET, J., SENIOR: 3 DAYS. He does not move. 'I was told he went to Carrow for work,' he says at last. 'Thirty years, I've been running brandy under the place he was lying in.' He gives the ledger back with both hands. 'The Company never paid him,' he says, and laughs, and it is a bad laugh. 'Three days. I should like them paid.'".
    On discuss { Assert ticked(party). }
  }
  Topic dunstan_names with dunstan "Read Dunstan the fourteen names from the Foreman's ledger" when holding(actor, carr_ledger) and not namesRead(party) once {
    Says "You read them. Dunstan sits quite still. At the sixth name, which is his own, struck through in a different ink because Carr thought he had gone up the shaft alive, he lifts his head. 'I did,' he says. 'I did go up. I have been dead six and fifty years, and nobody has said.' He takes the ledger and reads the fourteen aloud himself, slowly, to the room, and Hester Pook, at her pots, says each after him. Afterwards he pins the page to the beam beside the tokens.".
    On discuss { Assert namesRead(party). }
  }
  Observe names_pinned at taproom when namesRead(party) "Beside the Company's tokens, pinned to the beam, a page from a ledger: fourteen names, and by each of them, in Hester's hand, a day's wage in pence, paid.".
  Action read_names(actor: group, site: place) "Read the fourteen names aloud over the stacked dead" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ossuary) and at(ghouls, ossuary) and able(ghouls) and holding(actor, carr_ledger).
    Time 0.
    On success { Slay ghouls. Assert laid(party). }
    Result "You read them: the first name to the boy in the first boots, the last to the Foreman, slowly, as clerks do. At the ninth, the long hands lie down. At the fourteenth, no one in the vault is eating. They have been waiting, you think, only to be counted.".
  }

  Milestone m_names "had the fourteen counted" worth 200 when namesRead(party) or ticked(party) or laid(party).
}
